    "created_at": "2023-08-24T12:10:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-08-24T12:10:57Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I think the correct long term answer here is that blobs have an internal type slot that is either a MIME type or null. When Fetch serializes that it either gets a valid MIME type or the empty byte sequence.\r\n\r\n(At least, I think elsewhere we already settled on using the empty byte sequence as `Content-Type` value. And while that's not great, it's also not the worst. Certainly much better than `invalid`.)",
